{
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "$id": "urn:hsvg:2.0:schema:capability:page",
  "title": "HyperSVG 2.0 capability page: Page mascot",
  "description": "the settings under addons.page of the experience (D31): hooks (a name to a kind, optional, and for a spot floor, anchorX, edgeMarginPx, bodyClearancePx and priority), feet, actorPx, dock, idleMs and promptLimit (A3.1) | hook kinds: spot (stand on it), surface (walk along its top edge), target (point, highlight, scroll, signals, focus), control (invoke), grab (pick up and give back), obstacle (keep clear); hook names are id-grammar words; floor, anchorX, edgeMarginPx, bodyClearancePx and priority belong to spots only; defaults: floor bottom, priority 0, dock bottom-right 16 px inset 96 px size at 600 px phone breakpoint, idleMs 30000, promptLimit 3 per 600000 ms | placement: feet go to [x + w * anchorX, y + (floor is bottom ? h : 0)] of the spot box; the measured body must fit between the edge margins and clear every obstacle grown by bodyClearancePx; a spot that fails is skipped for the next by priority, else the actor docks; at or below phoneBreakpointPx the actor stays docked | signals in (each granted), heard as page:<signal> (page:clicked:<hook>, page:idle): visible and hidden at half a target's box, clicked, invalid, scrollEnd, idle, exitIntent (fine pointer through the top edge, never touch), scroll with {progress}; payloads hold only a hook name or a progress number | the output hookHealth and the ambient hooks input report each hook as found, missing or ambiguous | page actions out are the calls page.point and page.highlight {hook, durationMs}, page.scroll, page.focus and page.invoke {hook}; a point or highlight ends with page:ended:<action id> {interrupted}; page.invoke is humanOnly",
